<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achaemenid Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Achaemenids, first Persian Empire, Achaemenid dynasty, Achaemenid Persian Empire, Achaemenid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Achaemenid Empire was the first Persian Empire, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> in the sixth century BCE and stretching at its height from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>. It governed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapies</a>, royal roads and a policy of tolerating local customs and religions. It absorbed the Median, Babylonian and Egyptian realms and was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in the 330s BCE, influencing later states such as the Seleucid and Sasanian empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire.jpg" alt="Achaemenid Empire" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cattette · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Achaemenid_Empire_500_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
